From: iOSPlus10 ios26 port
Subject: [PATCH 0006] negroni SoC drivers (bsd/dev) on xnu-12377, as they are

The 48 bsd/dev/negroni_*.c drivers and their headers of the iOS 16 port (UFS, keys, touch, USB/ECM + command
server + live log, reboot/PON, RTC, SPMI, RPMh, ADSP/audio/TFA amps, SLPI, charger/battery/glink, thermal, cpufreq,
haptics, camera, fingerprint, DSI/DPU, Adreno kernel side, Wi-Fi/WLAN stack, Bluetooth, SMMU) copied unchanged
from the iOS 16 reference tree (scripts/ios26/ios16-ref-tree.sh = xnu-8796 + slop + patches/xnu up to 0385),
with one change for 12377:
- kmem_alloc/kmem_free/KMA_* moved from <vm/vm_kern.h> to <vm/vm_kern_xnu.h> in 12377: the 18 drivers that use
  them include <vm/vm_kern_xnu.h>.
- bsd/conf/files: the driver list (no pthread, HFS or AMFI lines: those families need rework).
- bsd/dev/negroni_weak_iokit.c (new): weak defaults for the 25 hooks the drivers call in the not yet ported
  IOKit drivers (Backlight/DSI, Framebuffer/fingerprint overlay, HID, GPU, WLAN interface) and in exception.c
  (process sampler).
[V] 2026-10-27: every driver compiles with Xcode 27.1 and the kernel links (scripts/ios26/kernel-make.sh).
Not tested on the phone. Each driver's 12377 behaviour (kmem flags, thread_call, mbuf KPIs) still needs a run.

