+/*
+ * NEGRONI (OnePlus 10 Pro 5G, SM8450 "waipio"): camera bring-up, levels 1-6 (patches 0310-0316).
+ *
+ * Boot-arg negronicam (default 0 = no camera register access at all):
+ *   1  level 1 (0310): GCC camera clocks, camcc titan top GDSC, camcc AHB/CAMNOC/CCI0 clocks from the
+ *      19.2 MHz TCXO, CCI0 controller reset. Proof: CCI hardware version + reset-done ack. Then all off.
+ *   2  level 2 (0311): level 1 + the rear main sensor (slot 0, Sony IMX789) power-up sequence, CCI0
+ *      master 0 pins, chip-ID read (7-bit 0x1a, register 0x0016, 2 bytes, expected 0x0789), then the
+ *      vendor power-down sequence and level 1 off. Nothing stays powered.
+ *   3  level 3 (0312): level 2 + CPAS top / CAMNOC (titan version, IFE_RDI_WR QoS from cpastop_v680_110.h,
+ *      error logger) + the apps-SMMU check of the camera streams (IFE, ICP): bypass, translate or fault.
+ *   4  level 4 (0313): level 3 + the capture clocks (camcc PLL0 1200 MHz and PLL3 864 MHz under an RPMh
+ *      mxc.lvl NOM vote; CPHY_RX/CSI1PHYTIMER/CSID 400 MHz, IFE0 432 MHz; IFE0 GDSC) + CSIPHY1 in C-PHY
+ *      mode, 3 trios (lane assign 0x0210), the csiphy-v2.1.0 tables of cam_csiphy_2_1_0_hwreg.h.
+ *      0314: then the IMX789 factory-test (FTM) register table, which ends with stream on (0x0100 = 1):
+ *      4000x3008 RAW10 (2x2 binned), C-PHY 3 trios, 30 fps; proof = the sensor frame counter (0x0005) moves.
+ *   5  level 5 (0315): level 4 + CSID0 (csid680) + IFE0 (vfe680) RDI0 write master into a physically
+ *      contiguous buffer below 4 GiB (frame-based WM, apps-SMMU bypass from level 3). First one frame from the
+ *      test pattern generator TPG13 (640x480 RAW10 colour bars, no sensor), then one IMX789 frame (FTM
+ *      mode, 4000x3008 RAW10). Proof: CSID BUF_DONE for RDI0 + the first bytes + a byte histogram.
+ *      The frames stay readable as /dev/negronicam-tpg and /dev/negronicam-sensor (64-byte header +
+ *      MIPI RAW10 bytes; scripts/camera/pull-frame.sh, scripts/camera/raw-to-png.py).
+ *   6  level 6 (0316): level 5 + the ICP (LX7) firmware CAMERA_ICP.mdt/.bNN from the ADSP firmware area
+ *      (scripts/audio/mkadsparea.py adds them; scripts/camera/extract-icp-fw.sh) into camera_region
+ *      0x9f500000 + 8 MiB, TrustZone PAS id 33 (init image, mem setup, auth and reset, lx7_core.c:619-663),
+ *      then the HFI handshake of hfi.c cam_hfi_init (queue table, INIT_REQUEST, INIT_RESPONSE) and
+ *      HFI_CMD_SYS_INIT -> HFI_MSG_SYS_INIT_DONE. PAS shutdown at power down.
+ *   negronicam_src=1|2|3  1 TPG only (no sensor power, all capture clocks at 19.2 MHz TCXO), 2 sensor only,
+ *      3 (default) both. negronicam_drate=N C-PHY data-rate table index (default 0, 0..11),
+ *      negronicam_settle=N settle count (default 52 = module file mode 1 settle, see l4_csiphy).
+ *   negronicam_pause=N  ms between steps (default 0, max 2000), for a camera on the screen log.
+ *   negronicam_votes=0|1  (0312, default 1, every level) before the first camcc access: RPMh mmcx.lvl NOM
+ *      (the titan GDSC parent pm8350c_s2_mmcx_voter_level) and the BCM votes of the camera NoC paths:
+ *      CN0 (cam_ahb: apps -> qhs_camera_cfg), MM1 + MM0 + SH0 + MC0 (cam_hf_0: qnm_camnoc_hf -> qns_mem_noc_hf ->
+ *      qns_llcc -> ebi). The votes stay after the run (a lower vote from this DRV could replace a boot vote).
+ *   negronicam_smmu=0|1|2|3  0 report only, 1 stop before DMA when a camera stream would fault or
+ *      translate through a context this kernel did not set up, 2 add a bypass SMR/S2CR pair for the stream
+ *      group (as negroniwlan_smmu=2, patch 0263) and remove it again at power down, 3 (0317; opt-in, not
+ *      the default since 2026-10-27) an apps-SMMU stage-1 context of ours (negroni_smmu_s1.c, 0249) for the IFE stream
+ *      0x800/0x460 (and, at level 6, the four ICP entries of live.dts:22629): frame and HFI buffers anywhere
+ *      in RAM, mapped at 32-bit IOVAs inside Android's windows (live.dts:22583-22672). Policy 1 is the
+ *      default at every level (levels 5+ then stop at the buffer). Why 3: XNU RAM starts at 0x840000000, so no buffer has a 32-bit physical
+ *      address, and Gunyah turns S2CR bypass into fault (README-wifi.md "2026-10-26 panic fix").
+ * Every step logs "NEGRONI CAM: step N NAME" and "... ok (T us)" or "... failed: reason". A failure
+ * powers down, in the vendor order, everything this file turned on; every wait is bounded.
+ * Runs in its own kernel thread: boot does not wait for it.
+ *
+ * Sources ([V], file:line):
+ *   live.dts  out/live.dts (dtc of ~/op10-backup/device/live.dtb, the phone's running DT)
+ *   camcc     OnePlus kernel drivers/clk/qcom/camcc-waipio.c (out/src/op-kernel, e9da592)
+ *   gcc       OnePlus kernel drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-waipio.c
+ *   gdsc      OnePlus kernel drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc-regulator.c
+ *   branch    OnePlus kernel drivers/clk/qcom/clk-branch.c, rcg = clk-rcg2.c
+ *   pinctrl   OnePlus kernel drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-waipio.h, pinctrl-msm.c
+ *   cci-dn    OnePlus camera-kernel drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_cci/ (out/src/op-modules):
+ *             cam_cci_hwreg.h, cam_cci_dev.h, cam_cci_soc.c, cam_cci_core.c
+ *   cci-up    Linux drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c (out/src/linux, torvalds 5b0764a)
+ *   csiphy    OnePlus camera-kernel drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_csiphy/cam_csiphy_core.c (START_DEV order
+ *             :2379-2429), include/cam_csiphy_2_1_0_hwreg.h (tables), cam_csiphy_dev.h:63-70 (lane bits)
+ *   pll       OnePlus kernel drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c (Lucid EVO: :200-213 offsets, :2969-3057
+ *             configure, :3059-3105 enable/disable), camcc-waipio.c:72-81 (PLL0) :321-329 (PLL3)
+ *   csid      Linux drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-680.c (out/src/linux) and camera-kernel
+ *             cam_isp/isp_hw_mgr/isp_hw/ife_csid_hw/cam_ife_csid680.h, cam_ife_csid_hw_ver2.c
+ *   vfe       Linux camss-vfe-680.c and camera-kernel vfe_hw/vfe17x/cam_vfe680.h (bus client 24 = RDI0),
+ *             vfe_bus/cam_vfe_bus_ver3.c (RDI MIPI RAW10 frame-based WM :856-870, start_wm :1398-1465)
+ *   tpg       camera-kernel cam_sensor_module/cam_tpg/tpg_hw/tpg_hw_v_1_3/tpg_hw_v_1_3.c (qcom,cam-tpg103)
+ *   icp       camera-kernel cam_icp/icp_hw/lx7_hw/lx7_core.c, lx7_reg.h, cam_icp/hfi.c (cam_hfi_init
+ *             :733-950, hfi_write_cmd, hfi_read_message), fw_inc/hfi_reg.h, fw_inc/hfi_sys_defs.h,
+ *             icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c cam_icp_mgr_hfi_init (event mode 0 = INTR_MODE)
+ *   cpas      OnePlus camera-kernel drivers/cam_cpas/cpas_top/cam_cpastop_hw.c, cpastop_v680_110.h
+ *   smmu      live.dts:15350-15370 apps-smmu@15000000, 22583-22672 msm_cam_smmu_ife / _icp
+ *   ftm       OnePlus camera-kernel drivers/oplus/cam_sensor_module/cam_sensor/cam_sensor_settings.h:6017-6141
+ *             (.imx789_setting, 116 writes, word address, byte data), written by cam_ftm_power_up
+ *             (oplus_cam_sensor_core.c:239-289, :441-449) with nothing else after the power-up
+ *   module    /odm/lib64/camera/com.qti.sensormodule.waipio.semco_imx789_MP.bin, decoded by
+ *             scripts/camera/cammodule.py into out/camera/modules.txt:43-50
+ *
+ * Clock choice: every camcc source used here has a 19.2 MHz TCXO entry F(19200000, P_BI_TCXO, 1, 0, 0)
+ * (camcc:955 camnoc_axi, 988 cci, 1257 fast_ahb, 1587 mclk, 1926 slow_ahb), so no camcc PLL is
+ * programmed. The DT asks 37.5 MHz (PLL0) for the CCI (live.dts:22056); at 19.2 MHz this file uses the
+ * Linux 19.2 MHz standard-mode (100 kHz) timing (cci-up:255-265), the table that Linux also selects
+ * for "qcom,sm8450-cci" (cci-up:871) when the CCI clock is 19.2 MHz. MCLK 19.2 MHz is the DT rate
+ * (live.dts:22206 clock-rates 0x124f800).
+ * Votes (0312, negronicam_votes=1, the default): before the first camcc access this file votes RPMh
+ * mmcx.lvl NOM and the BCMs of the camera NoC paths (l0_votes). 0310/0311 had no votes and relied on the
+ * UEFI display keeping MMCX and the config NoC up [I]; a camcc/CCI access without the NoC path up hangs the
+ * bus without an error. A vote from this DRV replaces this DRV's earlier vote for the same resource, so
+ * the levels chosen are at or above what the display needs [I], and they are not dropped after the run.
+ * The CCI is polled; its GIC line (SPI 0x1cc, live.dts:22061) stays disabled.
+ */
